  "solution": {
    "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><msub><mi>OCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> effect so, ring activating group and ortho para directing.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo></math> hyperconjugation &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> so, ring activating group (ortho para directing).<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>NH</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Here the aniline is the least reactive due to formation of anilinium ion in acidic medium. It will now act as strong <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> group.<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi>Cl</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math> so, ring deactivating &amp; meta directing.&nbsp;<br />&nbsp;",
